HST Office: the ribbon lays each tab out from one fixed chain of steps (owner decision 15/11/2026, gap list G10).

fitByPriority collapsed the least used groups first, reopened collapsed groups out of order and grew the others
back in priority order: a wider window could hide a label or collapse a group that a narrower one showed. Each
tab now has one chain of steps built from its groups' widths and usage, every step the one that saves the most
room for its cost (medium 0.2, labels 1, the button 3 per 100 px hidden, times the usage weight 1..4); a width
takes the shortest part of the chain that fits, so labels and groups only go as the window narrows.

